version: 0_3_4
status: low-latency ESP MJPEG transport candidate
previous_version: 0_3_3
passed_baseline: 0_2_4
notes: The owner explicitly requested the next patch after V033 to improve physical ESP32-CAM streaming speed and reduce latency. V034 preserves V033's PC-controlled idle/config/start/stop session model but replaces repeated one-JPEG-per-HTTP /capture polling with one persistent ESP :81/stream MJPEG connection. PC Studio sends a target stream FPS with the complete OV2640 settings, the ESP caps production at that rate, and the backend continuously ingests newest JPEGs into the existing CameraFrameService. Camera Sources uses a backend MJPEG preview so browser display no longer waits for React camera-status polling. Wi-Fi power save remains disabled and the ESP continues CAMERA_GRAB_LATEST with two PSRAM framebuffers. Simulation closes/pauses the active image stream and reopens it when simulation stops. V033 connect-with-zero-image-transfer behavior and legacy raw upload remain compatible. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road traffic control remains disabled.
